<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The splash screen's icon: iOS's LaunchScreen.storyboard, which is the launch animation's
     first frame — `coin1` (the white disc and the slot's black wedge) at 30 dp, the yellow coin at
     0.7 of it in its centre, and the slot's shading (`coin3`) at 0.63 of it at the lower left.
     LaunchAnimation starts from exactly these pieces at this size and place, so the hand-off from
     the splash has no seam. Yellow in dark mode too, as on iOS.

     **One image of the whole 288 dp canvas** (drawable-xxxhdpi/launch_splash_frame.png, rendered
     from iOS's pieces), with the art in the central 192 dp the platform masks a splash icon to.
     The system draws the icon at a base size of its own and scales the result, so the icon has to
     scale as one piece: as a layer list of fixed-size pieces it came up several times too big and
     snapped down to 30 dp when the app drew, and percentage insets misreport the drawable's size.
     The coin is in the splash's own yellow rather than iOS's `coin4`, a shade off it. -->
<bitmap xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:src="@drawable/launch_splash_frame"
    android:filter="true"
    android:gravity="fill" />
